A||N||3||Wolfhound||Fiberglass work||||5
Z||000000||Wolfhound||11-01-1999||07:18 AM||||Are the hood and deck actually fiberglass or as I understand a fiberglass reinforced plastic other than polyester resin.<BR> Will polyester resin bond with the deck composite and if not what will. I have an 87 blue GT that is going to be repainted original color. I have an extra hood that I want to vent and paint at the same time to be sure the paint matches.<BR> Any info appreciated! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||mutfish||11-01-1999||08:48 PM||||The hood,decklid,top and upper quarter panels are made of "sheet molded compound",the front and rear facias are "reaction injected molded urethane",the doors and the lower panels behind them are "reinforced reaction injection molded urethane"and the rocker panels are made from"thermo plastic olefin. As far as repairing the sheet molded parts I use fiberglass resin and polyester body filler with no problems.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||11-01-1999||08:59 PM||||I have been told that there are special repair procedures for SMC components. But in over ten years of auto refinishing, I have never used anything except regular fiberglass resin and body filler on these pieces. Plastic body filler can be used to repair other plastic body panels and bumper covers also with proper surface prep.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Wolfhound||11-01-1999||09:03 PM||||Thanks, I was unsure of the bond between the two. I really like the idea of improving the airflow for the radiator that I found in the forum. I intent to take a shot at it.||||reg||1
